The problem is that when `mri` parses `--base-url https://gitlab.com`, it returns `parsed` as:
```
{
  _: [],
  'base-url': 'https://gitlab.com'
}
```

The camelcase conversion turns this into `baseUrl`, so the parsed object has `baseUrl: 'https://gitlab.com'`.

But then when we set defaults, we set BOTH `baseUrl` AND `b` to `https://github.com`.

Then when we set parsed values, we only set `baseUrl` (because that's what the camelcase conversion of `base-url` gives us), but `b` remains as the default value.

The fix is to NOT set defaults for alias names that are not the "primary" name of the option. Or better yet, set defaults AFTER parsing, but only for names that weren't set by parsing.

