All 7 tests pass. Let me provide a summary of the fix:

## Summary

**Problem:** When an option has multiple names/aliases (e.g., `-b, --base-url`) and a default value, the default was incorrectly applied to all alias names even when one alias was already parsed.

**Root Cause:** In `CAC.ts`'s `mri` method:
1. mri parses `--base-url https://gitlab.com` and returns `{ b: 'https://gitlab.com' }` (resolves to primary/shortest name)
2. Defaults are set for ALL alias names: `b = 'https://github.com'`, `baseUrl = 'https://github.com'`
3. Parsed values are set: `b = 'https://gitlab.com'` (overwrites default for `b`)
4. But `baseUrl` retains the default value `'https://github.com'` — **BUG!**

**Fix:** After setting the parsed value for a key, propagate that value to ALL alias names of the same option:

```typescript
// Propagate the parsed value to all alias names of the same option
for (const cliOption of cliOptions) {
  if (cliOption.names.includes(key)) {
    for (const name of cliOption.names) {
      options[name] = parsed[key]
    }
  }
}
```

This ensures when one alias is parsed, all aliases receive the same value instead of some getting the default.

